# ix built by ix (docs/plans/plan_mkfiles.md): what every mkfile shares.
# The tools are the installed ones (make install, or PATH=$TOP/bin:$PATH):
# mini-mk reads this, mini-ml, mini-lex, mini-yacc, mini-cc, mini-asm,
# mini-ar and mini-ld do the work. Included after TOP is set.
# The recipes are rc's, on Linux too (mini-rc: MKSHELL=mini-rc in the
# environment, as kernels/9pi's Makefile and tests/lite.sh give it;
# mini-mk's own default on Plan 9), so that mini-9pi builds ix from
# the same mkfiles (docs/plans/plan_self_hosting.md).

# (what depends on the system is mkfiles/config.rc's, rc's work: a
# backquote each was an rc and an echo, read by every mini-mk)
# TOOLPRE, the tools' names: mini-ml on Linux, ml on mini-9pi's card,
# which sets $objtype as Plan 9 does (its mk reads it; Linux has none);
# O, the machine: 7 (arm64) or 5 (arm), as Plan 9's letters; on Plan 9
# its own, by $objtype; OS (below)
<|. $TOP/mkfiles/config.rc machine
# (MLOPT: mini-ml's optimizations, config.rc's: -O3 unless MLOPT is set)
ML=${TOOLPRE}ml -m $O $MLOPT
CC=${TOOLPRE}cc -m $O
AS=${TOOLPRE}asm -m $O
AR=${TOOLPRE}ar
LD=${TOOLPRE}ld -m $O -map
LEX=${TOOLPRE}lex
YACC=${TOOLPRE}yacc
# (for the shell's commands: walk, Plan 9's find; rc, for mkfiles/units.rc;
# mk, for a directory's builds by another's)
WALK=${TOOLPRE}walk
RC=${TOOLPRE}rc
MK=${TOOLPRE}mk

# the system the programs are for: linux, or plan9 (plan_rio.md: for
# mini-9pi; arm only today: mini-mk O=5 OS=plan9), its executables
# Plan 9's a.out (LDH, mini-ld -H2); on Plan 9 its own (config.rc)
# B: what is made goes there, not beside the sources: dune reads those
# directories too, and would take a Parser.ml for a source; Plan 9's
# beside Linux's (_mk/5-plan9). UNIXDIR, P9DIR and RTSRC: below.
<|. $TOP/mkfiles/config.rc system
L=$B/lib_core

# the stdlib's units, in the order they are linked and initialized
# (lib_core/units.txt's), and ix's own library's
STD=Pervasives Int32 Int64 Seq List Char Uchar String Bytes Array Sys Hashtbl Filename Obj Stack Queue \
 Buffer Marshal Printf Format Arg Gc Digest Random Callback Lexing Parsing Printexc Option Result Either Int Bool Float Fun \
 In_channel Out_channel Fpath Cap CapSys CapStdlib Logs Logs_fmt Unix CapUnix \
 Atomic Thread Mutex Condition Event
# (their names, as they are linked; lib_core/mkfile says where each one's
# file is: commons/ but Sys_plan9's on Plan 9 (P9DIR), and Source's,
# which is concurrency/Source.ml: commons/Source.ml is OCaml's threads')
COMMONS=Common I64 Binary Utf8 Console Logging Procs Json Set_ Map_ Regex Sys_plan9 Exception Exit Arg_ Fpath_ Chan FS Source
STDDIRS=core base collections printing parsing system concurrency commons
# (Unix is the system's: Linux's in system/, Plan 9's in system/plan9/,
# with an interface of its own, found first: UNIXDIR; and Sys_plan9,
# Plan 9's own for ix's programs, nothing elsewhere: P9DIR)
STDI=-I $TOP/lib_core/$UNIXDIR ${STDDIRS:%=-I $TOP/lib_core/%}
# their objects (a recipe is the shell's: ${X:%=...} is mk's, done here),
# kept in a library: a program links the units it uses (mini-ml -start
# names them all, weakly: Link.weak), not the 69
# old: STDOBJS=${STD:%=$L/%.$O} ${COMMONS:%=$L/%.$O}
# each program all of the stdlib: mini-rm 885 KB, its link 54 MB alive
STDUNITS=${STD:%=$L/%.$O} ${COMMONS:%=$L/%.$O}
STDOBJS=$L/lib_core.a
STDEND=$L/std_exit.$O $L/runtime.$O $L/libc.a
# RTSRC (config.rc): mini-ml's runtime's sources, runtime.c, the one
# file compiled, the parts it includes (gc.c, io.c...) and its headers
